  "note": "Independent producer-change maintenance rejudgment (2026-11-22): preserve ENFORCED and all 16 tag bindings / 9 code-map producers at the previous bounded scope. Independently inspected RFC 9494 Sections 4.3-4.4, bestpath.go::compareBeforeMED, bestpath.go::comparePairWithReason, rib_commands.go::extractCandidate, reactor_notify.go::Reactor.notifyMessageReceiverFrom and Reactor.notifyOneMessage, and the RIB and reactor LLGR tests. Working-tree change in compareBeforeMED (and comparePairWithReason) only inserts RFC 7611 Section 3 compareAcceptOwn(a, b) after Step 1 (LOCAL_PREF) and before compareAIGP/AS_PATH; Step 0 (stale-level depreference against storage.DepreferenceThreshold) and Step 1 (LOCAL_PREF) are byte-identical to HEAD, so any LLGR-stale route is still eliminated at Step 0 before LOCAL_PREF or ACCEPT_OWN is reached, while two LLGR-stale routes tie at Step 0 and proceed to normal tiebreaking per RFC 9494 Section 4.4. Also inspected the already-landed HEAD changes in reactor_notify.go (commits 44411d90c3, ed129f9e85: captured *Session / ConnectionID and RS-client filtered-retention continuation args) and the shifted file SHA of rfc9494_llgr_ingress_meta_test.go (helper receiveThroughIngress updated with clock: source.clock; both tagged unit SHAs are byte-identical): session.localLLGR.Load() -> src.LLGRAdvertised -> ingress routeMeta delivery is unchanged. All other 6 cited producer functions and all 16 tagged unit SHAs are unchanged. This is a source maintenance rejudgment only: no tests or discrimination replays were run by this auditor, and the existing compareBeforeMED (and reactor_notify) revert records in rfc/discrimination/rfc9494/RFC9494-4.3-1.json still carry prior producer SHAs until main renews them. Prior scope limitations remain in full (self-attach and reactor metadata revert records prove producer reachability only, not normal-return semantic mutation; daemon negative uses paired guard mutation provenance; no whole-RFC conformance or egress replay/retention credit is claimed).",
